I relaunched the four "gold page only" tests at the right image resolution. The previous wake had run them at the wrong one, so they could not be compared with the earlier results. The new runs are going now and should finish around 02:25.

**What happened.** The previous wake launched these four tests without setting the image resolution. They ran at 451,584 pixels per page instead of 1,003,520, which the earlier all-pages runs used. "Gold page only" means the pages that don't hold the answer are removed. The tests run on the four finetunes that differ only in first-stage chunk length (256 vs 1,024 tokens), for two seeds. All four finished cleanly (1,500 questions each, every answer judged). I closed them as off-regime and kept their numbers as a side reading.

**What the side reading shows (not a decision).** The model first trained on 1,024-token chunks still loses even with the gold page alone:

| seed | gold page only, low resolution (judge accuracy ↑, longer-chunk minus shorter-chunk) | all 4 pages, right resolution |
|---|---|---|
| 42 | −6.3 pt [−8.6, −3.8] | −6.2 pt [−8.6, −3.9] |
| 43 | −4.7 pt [−7.0, −2.3] | −4.3 pt [−6.7, −1.8] |

- pt = 1 point of judge accuracy; brackets are 95% confidence intervals; 1,500 paired questions per row.
- Every source loses, at both seeds and both resolutions.
- This is consistent with the loss sitting inside each compressed page, not in reading several pages. It decides nothing until the right-resolution runs land.

**Other fixes this wake.**
- **Push alert:** it was stale. The remote branch matches local, with 0 commits waiting, so I deleted the alert.
- **Input-check gate:** it stays marked provisional, as the automatic checker asked. The check compared the two modes from the same code, so I re-checked recorded runs. Compressed and uncompressed runs get the same number of pages per question on 1,500/1,500, 1,500/1,500 and 500/500 questions. That counts pages; it does not prove they are the same pages.
- **Records:** I added a known-issues row for the missing resolution setting. I updated `docs/longdoc_diagnosis.md` and filed three tool complaints. The ledger has four garbled launch notes from a shell-loop mistake; corrected notes follow them.

**Next:** when the four runs end, I compare the two chunk lengths per seed. If the loss stays at 3 pt or more, the next test puts the model's chosen page in uncompressed.

